All these methods perform a specific action. 
They have the same method names within their respective classes, 
but their implementations differ depending on the object.

shows polymorphism because different game characters and items can perform the same action in 
different ways. For example, different characters can use their special moves, 
while different potions can produce different effects using the same method name.

For example, a attack() method can behave differently depending
on the character. A Warrior can perform a sword attack, 
a Mage can cast a magic attack, and an Archer can shoot an arrow. 
